{"progress":{"stage":"page","page":2,"paragraphs":["EXT. RIDGE ROAD - DAY","Wind comes down off the ridge in long flat gusts, pushing the grass one way and then, for no reason, the other.","A road climbs the ridge in switchbacks. Nobody has driven it since the washout, and the grass is taking it back.","MARA, 40s, walks it with a pack on and four days in her legs. She has the face of someone who fixes things and is never thanked.","DELACROIX, 50s, walks behind her with a paper map folded to the right square. He does not look at it. He looks at the road, and counts.","DELACROIX","Thirty-one.","They take the bend. Gravel lets go under Mara’s boot and goes quietly over the edge.","MARA","You don’t have to do that out loud.","DELACROIX","The map says forty. I’d like to know when it’s lying.","Cloud sits on the ridge above them like a lid somebody forgot to close.","MARA","How long has he been up there?","DELACROIX","Three weeks. On his own.","MARA","They said two.","DELACROIX","They say a lot of things.","The road ends at the washout, a bite taken out of the mountain. Mara stops where the road stops, then goes round it on the rock.","DELACROIX","Thirty-eight."]}}
